---
// A package, in three layers: the OpenMOCA mark beside what each part of it stands for.
// The mark is drawn inline in the theme's colours, so it follows light and dark mode, and every word stays text
// that people, search engines and AI answers can read. Top to bottom, the rows match the mark: the pin, then the
// three layers. On a narrow screen the mark sits above the list.
---

<figure class="package-layers not-content">
  <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="The OpenMOCA mark: three layers with one pin through them">
    <defs>
      <mask id="pl-mask-lower" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120">
        <rect width="120" height="120" fill="#fff" />
        <polygon points="60,35.04 102.24,56.16 102.24,61.92 60,83.04 17.76,61.92 17.76,56.16" fill="#000" stroke="#000" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        <polygon points="60,13.92 102.24,35.04 102.24,40.8 60,61.92 17.76,40.8 17.76,35.04" fill="#000" stroke="#000" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" />
      </mask>
      <mask id="pl-mask-middle" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="0" y="0" width="120" height="120">
        <rect width="120" height="120" fill="#fff" />
        <polygon points="60,13.92 102.24,35.04 102.24,40.8 60,61.92 17.76,40.8 17.76,35.04" fill="#000" stroke="#000" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" />
      </mask>
    </defs>
    <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" mask="url(#pl-mask-lower)">
      <polygon points="60,56.16 102.24,77.28 60,98.4 17.76,77.28" />
      <polygon points="17.76,77.28 60,98.4 60,104.16 17.76,83.04" />
      <polygon points="60,98.4 102.24,77.28 102.24,83.04 60,104.16" />
    </g>
    <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round" mask="url(#pl-mask-middle)">
      <polygon points="60,35.04 102.24,56.16 60,77.28 17.76,56.16" />
      <polygon points="17.76,56.16 60,77.28 60,83.04 17.76,61.92" />
      <polygon points="60,77.28 102.24,56.16 102.24,61.92 60,83.04" />
    </g>
    <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <polygon points="60,13.92 102.24,35.04 60,56.16 17.76,35.04" />
      <polygon points="17.76,35.04 60,56.16 60,61.92 17.76,40.8" />
      <polygon points="60,56.16 102.24,35.04 102.24,40.8 60,61.92" />
    </g>
    <line x1="60" y1="8.16" x2="60" y2="35.04" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4.2" stroke-linecap="round" />
    <circle cx="60" cy="7.66" r="4.6" fill="currentColor" />
    <line x1="60" y1="104.16" x2="60" y2="113.76" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="4.2" stroke-linecap="round" />
  </svg>
  <dl class="layers">
    <div class="layer trust">
      <dt>Trust <span>through all three</span></dt>
      <dd>One digest covers every file of the package, so any change shows. Signatures and reviews sit beside it: a
        signed package proves who published it, and signed reviews prove who checked which node.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="layer structure">
      <dt>Structure <span>optional</span></dt>
      <dd>Concepts and how they relate: hierarchy, parts, order, what requires what. W3C SKOS and DCMI terms, plus any
        vocabulary you add, such as an OWL ontology, carried as it is.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="layer content">
      <dt>Content</dt>
      <dd>The knowledge, one Markdown node per topic, with validity windows, audiences and translations.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="layer evidence">
      <dt>Evidence</dt>
      <dd>The original sources, carried in the package where they can be, and selectors that point into them, so a
        quote can be checked against the original.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</figure>

<style>
  .package-layers {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 15rem) 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .mark {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--moca-text);
  }
  .layers {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .package-layers .layers .layer {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--layer);
    padding-left: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .package-layers .layers .layer dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--layer);
    font-size: var(--moca-text-lg);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .layer dt span {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--moca-text-sm);
    color: var(--moca-text-muted);
    margin-left: 0.4rem;
  }
  .package-layers .layers .layer dd {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    margin-inline-start: 0;
    color: var(--moca-text);
  }
  .trust { --layer: var(--moca-pin); }
  .structure { --layer: var(--moca-structure); }
  .content { --layer: var(--moca-content); }
  .evidence { --layer: var(--moca-evidence); }

  @media (max-width: 50rem) {
    .package-layers {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .mark {
      width: 9rem;
      justify-self: center;
    }
  }
</style>
